{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":22704,"duration_api_ms":24020,"num_turns":8,"result":"I wrote the script at `src/cpufreq/cpufreq.bt`, but I haven't run it. I couldn't check that bpftrace is installed here.\n\nIt attaches to the `power:cpu_frequency` tracepoint. Each time a CPU's frequency changes, it prints a line with the time in ms, the CPU, and the old and new frequency in MHz. When you hit Ctrl-C, bpftrace prints these maps:\n- `@changes`: number of changes per CPU.\n- `@freq_hist_mhz`: a per-CPU histogram of the new frequency.\n- `@freq_avg_mhz`: the average new frequency across all CPUs.\n\nRun it with:\n```bash\nsudo bpftrace src/cpufreq/cpufreq.bt\n```\n\nThe old frequency shows 0 the first time a CPU is seen. The tracepoint only fires when a cpufreq driver is active. It may stay silent in some VMs or when the driver doesn't report frequency changes.\n\nI used the directory name `cpufreq` because I didn't know which tutorial number you want. Tell me the number and I'll rename it and add a README.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"eff69897-c203-4462-b92f-3203dc18ef0f","total_cost_usd":0.08645905000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":12,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2901,"cache_read_input_tokens":129811,"output_tokens":2410,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2901},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":374,"cache_read_input_tokens":27236,"cache_creation_input_tokens":943,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":943,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":351,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000451,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":